14
00:52:53,333 --> 00:52:59,333
Sense and Sensibility is a 1995 period drama film directed by Ang Lee
and based on Jane Austen's 1811 novel of the same name.

15
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Emma Thompson wrote the screenplay and stars as Elinor Dashwood, while
Kate Winslet plays Elinor's younger sister Marianne.

16
01:00:26,666 --> 01:00:32,666
The story follows the Dashwood sisters, members of a wealthy English family of landed
gentry, as they must deal with circumstances of sudden destitution.

17
01:04:13,333 --> 01:04:19,333
They are forced to seek financial security through marriage.

18
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Hugh Grant and Alan Rickman play their respective suitors.

19
01:11:46,666 --> 01:11:52,666
Producer Lindsay Doran, a long time admirer of Austen's
novel, hired Thompson to write the screenplay.

20
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
She spent five years drafting numerous revisions, continually working on the script
between other films as well as into production of the film itself.

21
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
Studios were nervous that Thompson—a first-time screenwriter—was the credited
writer, but Columbia Pictures agreed to distribute the film.

22
01:23:06,666 --> 01:23:12,666
Though initially intending to have another actress portray
Elinor, Thompson was persuaded to take the role.

23
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:59,333
Thompson's screenplay exaggerated the Dashwood family's wealth to make their
later scenes of poverty more apparent to modern audiences.

24
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
It also altered the traits of the male leads to make them
more appealing to contemporary viewers.

25
01:34:26,666 --> 01:34:32,666
Elinor and Marianne's different characteristics were
emphasised through imagery and invented scenes.

26
01:38:13,333 --> 01:38:19,333
Lee was selected as director, both for his work in the 1993 film The Wedding Banquet and
because Doran believed he would help the film appeal to a wider audience.

27
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
Lee was given a budget of $16 million.

28
01:45:46,666 --> 01:45:52,666
Sense and Sensibility was released on 13 December 1995, in the United States.

29
01:49:33,333 --> 01:49:39,333
A commercial success, earning $135 million worldwide, the film garnered overwhelmingly positive reviews upon release and
received many accolades, including three awards and eleven nominations at the 1995 British Academy Film Awards.

30
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:26,000
It earned seven Academy Awards nominations, including
for Best Picture and Best Actress.

31
01:57:06,666 --> 01:57:12,666
Thompson received the award for Best Adapted Screenplay, becoming the only
person to have won Academy Awards for both acting and screenwriting.

32
02:00:53,333 --> 02:00:59,333
Sense and Sensibility contributed to a resurgence in popularity for Austen's
works, and has led to many more productions in similar genres.

33
02:04:40,000 --> 02:04:46,000
It continues to be recognised as one of the best Austen adaptations of all time.

34
